{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The angel who redeems me from all evil, may he bless.</b> He directed that the angel who redeems him bless <b>the youths</b> — if they are not worthy of his blessing except through an intermediary." "<b>And may my name be called upon them, and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac.</b> Not the name of Terah and Nahor, for the righteous will not have the name of their wicked ancestors called upon them, and conversely, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 52a): we call a wicked person, even the son of a righteous person, 'wicked son of wicked,' so that he is not traced to his righteous father but to one of his wicked ancestors. Therefore he prayed for them that they be prepared and aided for the service of the blessed El, so that they be worthy of being traced to Abraham and to Isaac, in the manner of (Psalms 86:11) יַחֵד לְבָבִי לְיִרְאָה — 'unite my heart to fear' — אֶת שְׁמֶךָ."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:13.179458739Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}